Subject: Tweak: robot goalies
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Super Mario Strikers (GameCube) has a hidden robot team, the Super Team, whose
goalie is a Kritter in a robot skin. Charged's disc still holds that skin's
texture, art/characters/superteamgoalie/superteamgoalie.rlt, but no code loads
it: the goalie skin table has the twelve teams only, and the texture is laid
out for the GameCube Kritter, whose model Charged replaced.

With "Robot goalies" enabled, both goalies wear it. CharacterLoader passes each
goalie texture bundle as it loads (a team's kit, an away kit, also one Mirror
match made, and the shared bundle with the eye and shine mask) to the port,
which lays the robot texture onto Charged's goalie textures in place
(src/platform/robot_goalie.cpp, with the map of assets/gameplay). Only the look
changes; the goalie's model, animations and play are the game's.

diff --git a/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp b/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp
index 5ee1bf5..00c8116 100644
--- a/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp
@@ -204,6 +204,31 @@ static bool BluePeachTeam(eCharacterClass captain0, eCharacterClass captain1, in
 }
 #endif
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// Port tweak "Robot goalies": both goalies wear the robot goalie skin of the
+// Super Team from Super Mario Strikers. The disc still has its texture, unused
+// and laid out for that game's goalie; the port lays it onto every goalie
+// texture of a bundle as it loads (src/platform/robot_goalie.cpp).
+static void RobotGoalieTextures(void* data, unsigned long size)
+{
+    if (!mscharged_tweak_enabled(MSCHARGED_TWEAK_ROBOT_GOALIES) || data == 0)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    const char* szRobot = "art/characters/superteamgoalie/superteamgoalie.rlt";
+    unsigned long robotSize = 0;
+    void* robot = nlFileExists(szRobot) ? nlLoadEntireFile(szRobot, &robotSize, 32, AllocateStart, 0, 0, 0) : 0;
+    if (robot == 0 || mscharged_tweak_robot_goalie_textures(data, size, robot, robotSize) == 0)
+    {
+        nlPrintf("Robot goalies: a goalie texture bundle keeps its look\n");
+    }
+    if (robot != 0)
+    {
+        nlFree(robot);
+    }
+}
+#endif
+
 CharacterLoader::~CharacterLoader()
 {
 }
